          <div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item reveal"><summary class="faq-q">Is RestaBee suitable for a single-outlet restaurant?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-a">RestaBee supports restaurant order entry, kitchen tickets, tables, billing and reports. Book a demo using your own restaurant workflow to assess the fit.</div></details><details class="faq-item reveal"><summary class="faq-q">Can I take delivery orders?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Staff can enter delivery orders and permitted delivery or packaging charges. This is not automatic delivery-platform ingestion or courier tracking.</div></details><details class="faq-item reveal"><summary class="faq-q">Can I configure GST billing?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-a">RestaBee supports configured tax profiles and captured tax lines on bills. This does not include GST filing, government certification or e-invoicing integration.</div></details><details class="faq-item reveal"><summary class="faq-q">Which devices and printers can I use?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Confirm your intended devices and printers during the demo. Bill and kitchen-ticket printing requires compatible hardware and a local setup.</div></details><details class="faq-item reveal"><summary class="faq-q">Can I split bills and payments?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Eligible unissued checks can be arranged before billing. Collections can also be recorded across multiple payment methods. Split checks and split payments are separate controls.</div></details><details class="faq-item reveal"><summary class="faq-q">Can I manage several outlets?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Review central menu changes and apply published updates to selected outlets. Outlet-scoped staff permissions and independent local menus are supported.</div></details></div></div></section>
